2026-10-02T20:43:22.8209463Z ##[group]Run set -euo pipefail
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8209811Z set -euo pipefail
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8210170Z # --no-renames, and it is not cosmetic: a rename is reported by its
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8210655Z # DESTINATION only, so moving CLAUDE.md to RENAMED.md yields a list
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8211138Z # matching no glob and the approval gate would not fire on the change
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8211612Z # that removed a policy file. Measured both ways before wiring it.
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8212121Z git diff --no-renames --name-only "$PR_BASE...$PR_HEAD" > /tmp/pr-files.txt
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8212550Z wc -l < /tmp/pr-files.txt
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8212909Z # The same diff less its additions: what the base already had. A
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8213368Z # reporter that grades `main` is exempt from `## Red checks` only
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8213862Z # while the diff touches none of its inputs, and a delivery row the
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8214640Z # pull request ADDS (its own) is not one; a row it edits or deletes is.
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8215236Z git diff --no-renames --name-only --diff-filter=a "$PR_BASE...$PR_HEAD" > /tmp/pr-existing.txt
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8281032Z shell: /usr/bin/bash -e {0}
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8281290Z env:
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8281530Z   PR_BASE: 68b8cb97d911339a206fde141ecfdf0f57c6ccc4
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8281874Z   PR_HEAD: 9efd4dd4065492efd48d389ffe1827b1fe5b4a2b
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8282178Z ##[endgroup]
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8409241Z 21
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8474113Z ##[group]Run set -euo pipefail
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8474733Z set -euo pipefail
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8475115Z # Fail-closed, on the paths-file step's own principle: a derivation
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8475627Z # that fails must fail the step, because an empty red list read from
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8476105Z # a failed fetch is "no reds" -- the fail-open this wiring closes.
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8476494Z gh api --paginate \
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8476835Z   "repos/${GITHUB_REPOSITORY}/commits/${PR_HEAD}/check-runs" \
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8477224Z   --jq '.check_runs[]
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8477567Z          | select(.status == "completed" and .conclusion == "failure")
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8477962Z          | select(.name != "pr-contract")
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8478289Z          | .name' | sort -u > /tmp/pr-reds.txt
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8478679Z printf 'red checks the body must answer: %s\n' \
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8479030Z   "$(paste -sd, /tmp/pr-reds.txt)"
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8540117Z shell: /usr/bin/bash -e {0}
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8540371Z env:
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8543256Z   GH_TOKEN: ***
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8543526Z   PR_HEAD: 9efd4dd4065492efd48d389ffe1827b1fe5b4a2b
2026-10-02T20:43:22.8543834Z ##[endgroup]
2026-10-02T20:43:23.4608318Z red checks the body must answer: nightly-status
2026-10-02T20:43:23.4642413Z ##[group]Run set -euo pipefail
2026-10-02T20:43:23.4642752Z set -euo pipefail
2026-10-02T20:43:23.4643101Z # One --red flag per name, never one comma-joined value: a check
2026-10-02T20:43:23.4643587Z # name containing a comma would split into fragments neither the
2026-10-02T20:43:23.4643979Z # refusal nor `## Red checks` can match.
2026-10-02T20:43:23.4644588Z RED_ARGS=()
